            <ArticleTitle>Double omental hernia--case report on a very rare cause of intestinal obstruction.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>799-801</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="INTRODUCTION" NlmCategory="BACKGROUND">We report a case of transomental herniation of the ileum through a defect in the gastrocolic ligament with re-emergence through a defect in the gastrohepatic ligament. This type of herniation is extremely rare and a review of the literature is presented.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CLINICAL PRESENTATION" NlmCategory="METHODS">A 41-year-old Chinese male presented with signs and symptoms of intestinal obstruction.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="TREATMENT" NlmCategory="METHODS">An urgent laparotomy was undertaken and he was found to have a rare form of intra-abdominal hernia. The hernia was reduced and the defects were closed.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="OUTCOME" NlmCategory="RESULTS">Postoperative recovery was unremarkable.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSION" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">Urgent operation should not be delayed because of the high mortality associated with strangulation.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
